<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">title: "Kitchen Remodel Cost Breakdown: Real Numbers for Cabinets, Countertops &amp; Everything Else" description: "Complete kitchen renovation cost breakdown with actual material prices, labor rates, and where contractors inflate quotes. Budget from $15K to $75K+." date: 2024-01-17 author: Ungouge Team keywords: ["kitchen remodel cost breakdown", "kitchen renovation cost", "kitchen remodel budget", "how much does kitchen remodel cost", "kitchen renovation prices"]</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h1 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.1px 0.0px; font: 24.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #138756; -webkit-text-stroke: #138756"><span class="s1"><b>Kitchen Remodel Cost Breakdown: Real Numbers for Cabinets, Countertops &amp; Everything Else</b></span></h1>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">You want a new kitchen. You've gotten quotes ranging from $25,000 to $75,000 for what seems like the same work. How is that possible?</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Kitchen remodels are notorious for price opacity. There are dozens of line items, multiple materials to choose from, and enough complexity that contractors can bury inflated costs where most homeowners will never find them.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">This guide breaks down exactly what each component of a kitchen remodel should cost—from cabinets to countertops to the labor to install them. You'll know what's fair, what's padded, and where to push back.</span></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Kitchen Remodel Cost Overview by Size</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Before diving into itemized costs, here are realistic total budgets by kitchen size:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td1">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Kitchen Size</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td2">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Budget Remodel</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td3">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-Range Remodel</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td4">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>High-End Remodel</b></span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Small (70-100 sq ft)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$15,000-$25,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$25,000-$45,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$45,000-$75,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Medium (100-150 sq ft)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$25,000-$40,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$40,000-$65,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$65,000-$100,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td5">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Large (150-200+ sq ft)</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td6">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$40,000-$60,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td7">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$60,000-$90,000</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td8">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$90,000-$150,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What defines each tier:</b></span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget:</b> Stock cabinets, laminate countertops, basic appliances, vinyl flooring, minimal structural changes</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-Range:</b> Semi-custom cabinets, quartz or granite countertops, quality appliances, tile or engineered hardwood flooring, some layout changes</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>High-End:</b> Custom cabinets, premium countertops (marble, quartzite), high-end appliances, hardwood or luxury tile flooring, significant layout changes, designer lighting</span></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>The Itemized Breakdown: Where Your Money Goes</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Cabinets (30-40% of total budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Cabinets are the single largest expense in most kitchen remodels. The price variation is enormous.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Stock Cabinets (Budget)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $75-$200 per linear foot - <b>Total for 20 linear feet:</b> $1,500-$4,000 - Pre-manufactured, standard sizes - Limited styles and finishes - Particle board or MDF construction - Basic hardware included</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Brands:</b> IKEA, Hampton Bay (Home Depot), Continental Cabinets</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Semi-Custom Cabinets (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $150-$400 per linear foot - <b>Total for 20 linear feet:</b> $3,000-$8,000 - More size and finish options - Better construction (plywood boxes) - Soft-close hinges and drawer glides - Dovetail drawer construction</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Brands:</b> KraftMaid, Merillat, American Woodmark, Thomasville</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Custom Cabinets (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $500-$1,500+ per linear foot - <b>Total for 20 linear feet:</b> $10,000-$30,000+ - Any size, style, finish - Premium materials (solid wood, exotic veneers) - Hand-crafted details - Full customization</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Brands:</b> Local cabinet makers, Wood-Mode, Rutt, SieMatic</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Installation Labor</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $50-$100 per linear foot - <b>Total for 20 linear feet:</b> $1,000-$2,000 - Includes removal of old cabinets - Installation, leveling, securing - Hardware installation</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> If installation labor exceeds $125 per linear foot for standard cabinets, question it.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Countertops (10-15% of total budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Countertop pricing varies wildly by material, thickness, edge detail, and square footage.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Laminate (Budget)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $10-$40 per square foot installed - <b>50 sq ft kitchen:</b> $500-$2,000 - Affordable, many colors - Not heat-resistant - Can chip or peel over time</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Tile (Budget-Mid)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $15-$50 per square foot installed - <b>50 sq ft kitchen:</b> $750-$2,500 - Durable, heat-resistant - Grout lines require maintenance - Can be DIY-friendly</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Quartz (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $50-$120 per square foot installed - <b>50 sq ft kitchen:</b> $2,500-$6,000 - Non-porous, low maintenance - Consistent color and pattern - Not heat-proof (hot pans can damage)</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Brands:</b> Caesarstone, Cambria, Silestone</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Granite (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $40-$100 per square foot installed - <b>50 sq ft kitchen:</b> $2,000-$5,000 - Natural stone, unique patterns - Requires periodic sealing - Heat-resistant</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Marble (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $75-$250 per square foot installed - <b>50 sq ft kitchen:</b> $3,750-$12,500 - Luxurious, classic appearance - Stains and scratches easily - High maintenance</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Quartzite (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $70-$200 per square foot installed - <b>50 sq ft kitchen:</b> $3,500-$10,000 - Natural stone, hard as granite - Marble-like appearance - Requires sealing</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>What's Included in "Installed" Price</b></span></h4>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Template and measurement</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Fabrication (cutting, edge detail)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Delivery and installation</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Seam sealing (if applicable)</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Sink cutout (first one)</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flags:</b> - Charging separately for "template fee" ($200-$400) when quote says "installed" - Fabrication charges that double the material cost - Seam charges over $100 per seam - Edge detail upcharges over $20 per linear foot for standard edges</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. Flooring (5-10% of total budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Kitchen flooring must handle traffic, spills, and temperature changes.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Vinyl/LVP (Budget)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $2-$7 per square foot installed - <b>150 sq ft kitchen:</b> $300-$1,050 - Waterproof, durable - Easy installation (can be DIY) - Good for resale value</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Ceramic/Porcelain Tile (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $5-$15 per square foot installed - <b>150 sq ft kitchen:</b> $750-$2,250 - Highly durable, waterproof - Cold underfoot (can add radiant heat) - Professional installation recommended</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Engineered Hardwood (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $6-$16 per square foot installed - <b>150 sq ft kitchen:</b> $900-$2,400 - Real wood look, more stable than solid - Not fully waterproof - Refinishable (limited times)</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Solid Hardwood (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $8-$20 per square foot installed - <b>150 sq ft kitchen:</b> $1,200-$3,000 - Classic, timeless - Not recommended for kitchens (water damage risk) - Refinishable multiple times</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Installation labor typically:</b> $2-$5 per sq ft depending on complexity</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Charging $10+ per square foot for vinyl installation. Standard LVP installation is $2-$3 per sq ft.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Backsplash (2-5% of total budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Backsplash is where style meets function—and where costs can escalate quickly.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Ceramic Tile (Budget)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $7-$15 per square foot installed - <b>40 sq ft backsplash:</b> $280-$600 - Standard subway tile or simple patterns - Durable, easy to clean</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Glass Tile (Mid-Range)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $15-$40 per square foot installed - <b>40 sq ft backsplash:</b> $600-$1,600 - Reflective, modern look - More difficult to install (higher labor)</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Natural Stone/Marble (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $20-$60 per square foot installed - <b>40 sq ft backsplash:</b> $800-$2,400 - Luxurious appearance - Requires sealing - Can stain from cooking splatters</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Designer/Custom Tile (High-End)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $30-$100+ per square foot installed - <b>40 sq ft backsplash:</b> $1,200-$4,000+ - Handmade, artisan tiles - Unique patterns or mosaics - Labor-intensive installation</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Installation labor:</b> $5-$15 per sq ft depending on tile type and pattern complexity</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Simple subway tile installation labor over $8 per sq ft. Standard is $4-$6 per sq ft.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>5. Plumbing (5-10% of total budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Plumbing costs vary dramatically based on whether you're relocating fixtures or simply replacing them.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Sink Replacement (No Relocation)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $200-$600 - Disconnect old sink - Install new sink (undermount or drop-in) - Connect supply lines and drain - 2-4 hours of labor</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Faucet Installation</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $150-$350 - Remove old faucet - Install new faucet - Connect supply lines - Test for leaks - 1-2 hours of labor</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Garbage Disposal Installation</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $150-$400 - <b>Unit cost:</b> $75-$250 - <b>Labor:</b> $75-$150 - Electrical connection required - 1-2 hours</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Dishwasher Installation</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $150-$400 (labor only; appliance separate) - Connect water supply - Connect drain line - Level and secure unit - Test operation - 2-3 hours</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Relocating Plumbing (Major Cost)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $1,500-$5,000+ depending on distance - Rerouting water supply lines - Relocating drain pipes - May require opening walls/floors - Requires permits and inspections</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Typical plumber hourly rate:</b> $75-$150 per hour (varies by region)</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Charging $800 to install a sink when no relocation is involved. Standard installation is $200-$400.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>6. Electrical (5-10% of total budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Kitchens require significant electrical work: outlets, lighting, appliance circuits.</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Outlet Installation (Standard)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $100-$200 per outlet - Includes box, outlet, wiring (short run) - GFCI outlets (required in kitchens) - 1-2 hours per outlet</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Under-Cabinet Lighting</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $250-$800 total - LED strip lighting: $30-$60 per linear foot installed - Puck lights: $50-$100 per light installed - Hardwired vs plug-in affects cost</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Recessed Lighting</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $150-$300 per light installed - Includes fixture, housing, trim - Wiring to switch - Cutting ceiling holes - 2-3 hours per light</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Pendant/Chandelier Installation</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $100-$300 per fixture (labor only) - Mounting electrical box - Wiring to switch - Hanging and securing fixture - 1-2 hours per fixture</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Appliance Circuits (New)</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $300-$800 per circuit - 240V for range/oven: $400-$800 - 120V for dishwasher/disposal: $300-$500 - Running wire from panel to location - Dedicated circuit required by code</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Typical electrician hourly rate:</b> $75-$150 per hour (varies by region)</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Charging $500 to install a single standard outlet. Unless significant rewiring is needed, this is padding.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>7. Labor (20-35% of total budget)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Beyond specialized trades (plumber, electrician), general contractor labor includes:</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Demolition</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $1,000-$3,000 for average kitchen - Remove old cabinets, countertops, flooring - Disconnect appliances - Haul away debris - Dumpster rental: $400-$800</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Time:</b> 1-3 days depending on scope</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>Drywall Repair/Painting</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $1,500-$4,000 - Patching walls after cabinet removal - Skim coating/texturing - Priming and painting walls/ceiling - 2 coats of paint</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Typical painting cost:</b> $2-$6 per sq ft</span></p>
<h4 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 16.0px 0.0px; font: 12.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #262626; -webkit-text-stroke: #262626"><span class="s1"><b>General Carpentry</b></span></h4>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $50-$100 per hour - Trimwork and molding - Building custom shelving - Installing hardware - Miscellaneous adjustments</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> "Labor" line items without specifics. Insist on breakdown by task and estimated hours.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>8. Appliances (15-25% of budget if replacing all)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Appliance costs vary from basic to luxury:</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="t1">
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td9">
        <p class="p5"><span class="s1"><b>Appliance</b></span></p>
