        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$300-$600</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$600-$1,200</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$1,200-$2,500+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Microwave</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$100-$300</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$300-$800</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$800-$2,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td valign="middle" class="td13">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1"><b>Range Hood</b></span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td14">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$200-$500</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td15">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$500-$1,500</span></p>
      </td>
      <td valign="middle" class="td16">
        <p class="p6"><span class="s1">$1,500-$5,000+</span></p>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget package (all appliances):</b> $2,000-$4,000 <b>Mid-range package:</b> $4,000-$9,000 <b>High-end package:</b> $9,000-$30,000+</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Installation is typically extra:</b> $100-$400 per appliance</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> Contractors charging $800 to install a dishwasher or range. Standard installation is $150-$400 unless significant modifications are needed.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Small vs. Medium vs. Large Kitchen Budgets</b></span></h2>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Small Kitchen Remodel (70-100 sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget-conscious ($15,000-$25,000):</b> - Stock cabinets (12-15 linear ft): $2,500-$4,000 - Laminate countertops (30 sq ft): $600-$1,200 - Vinyl flooring (80 sq ft): $500-$800 - Ceramic tile backsplash (25 sq ft): $300-$500 - Budget appliances: $2,000-$3,500 - Basic plumbing/electrical updates: $1,500-$2,500 - Labor (demo, install, paint): $5,000-$8,000 - Permits/contingency: $1,600-$2,500</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range ($25,000-$45,000):</b> - Semi-custom cabinets: $4,500-$7,500 - Quartz countertops: $2,000-$3,500 - Luxury vinyl or tile flooring: $800-$1,500 - Glass or stone backsplash: $800-$1,500 - Mid-range appliances: $3,500-$6,000 - Plumbing/electrical upgrades: $2,500-$4,000 - Labor: $7,500-$12,000 - Permits/contingency: $3,400-$9,000</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Medium Kitchen Remodel (100-150 sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget-conscious ($25,000-$40,000):</b> - Stock cabinets (18-22 linear ft): $3,500-$6,000 - Laminate/tile countertops (45 sq ft): $1,000-$2,000 - Vinyl flooring (120 sq ft): $700-$1,200 - Ceramic backsplash (35 sq ft): $400-$700 - Budget appliances: $2,500-$4,000 - Plumbing/electrical: $2,000-$3,500 - Labor: $8,000-$13,000 - Permits/contingency: $3,900-$7,600</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range ($40,000-$65,000):</b> - Semi-custom cabinets: $6,000-$10,000 - Quartz/granite countertops: $3,000-$5,500 - Tile or engineered hardwood: $1,200-$2,400 - Designer backsplash: $1,000-$2,000 - Mid-range appliances: $4,000-$7,000 - Plumbing/electrical: $3,500-$5,500 - Labor: $12,000-$19,000 - Permits/contingency: $5,300-$13,600</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Large Kitchen Remodel (150-200+ sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Budget-conscious ($40,000-$60,000):</b> - Stock cabinets (25-30 linear ft): $5,000-$8,000 - Laminate/quartz countertops (60 sq ft): $1,500-$4,000 - Vinyl/basic tile flooring (180 sq ft): $1,200-$2,000 - Backsplash (50 sq ft): $600-$1,200 - Budget appliances: $3,000-$5,000 - Plumbing/electrical: $3,000-$5,000 - Labor: $15,000-$22,000 - Permits/contingency: $6,700-$12,800</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Mid-range ($60,000-$90,000):</b> - Semi-custom cabinets: $8,000-$14,000 - Quartz/granite countertops: $4,000-$7,000 - Quality tile or hardwood: $2,000-$3,500 - Designer backsplash: $1,500-$3,000 - Mid-range appliances: $5,000-$8,000 - Plumbing/electrical with upgrades: $4,500-$7,500 - Labor: $20,000-$30,000 - Permits/contingency: $10,000-$17,000</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>High-end ($90,000-$150,000+):</b> - Custom cabinets: $15,000-$40,000+ - Premium countertops (marble, quartzite): $6,000-$15,000 - Hardwood or luxury tile: $3,500-$6,000 - Custom backsplash: $2,500-$6,000 - High-end appliances: $9,000-$25,000 - Extensive plumbing/electrical: $7,000-$12,000 - Labor: $25,000-$40,000 - Permits/contingency: $15,000-$30,000</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Where Contractors Pad Quotes the Most</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Based on analysis of thousands of quotes, here's where padding is most common:</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Labor Hours</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Quoting 80 hours for cabinet installation that should take 20.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Ask for task-specific labor estimates and compare to industry standards.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Material Markups</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Charging $8,000 for cabinets they purchased for $3,000.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Research the specific products they're quoting and verify retail prices. Reasonable markup is 20-40%.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. "Project Management" Fees</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Adding 15-20% "project management" on top of general contractor fees.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> GC overhead should be built into their rates, not an extra line item. If it's separate, it should be 5-10% max and clearly defined.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Vague Contingency</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> 20% contingency that's never itemized or returned if unused.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Contingency should be 10-15% max and only charged if issues arise (with documentation).</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>5. Inflated Demo Costs</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> $4,000 for demolition that takes one day with a 2-person crew.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Demo typically costs $1,000-$2,500 for average kitchen. If it's higher, ask why.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>6. Permit Fees</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>The scam:</b> Charging $1,200 for permits that actually cost $300.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How to catch it:</b> Call your local building department and ask what permits are required and their cost.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Money-Saving Tips That Don't Sacrifice Quality</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">You can reduce costs without compromising the integrity of your remodel:</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>1. Keep the Layout</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Moving plumbing and electrical is expensive ($3,000-$10,000+). If you can work with your existing layout, you'll save significantly.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>2. Reface Instead of Replace Cabinets</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">If your cabinet boxes are solid, refacing (new doors, drawer fronts, veneering the frames) costs 40-50% less than full replacement.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Cost:</b> $4,000-$9,000 vs. $8,000-$20,000 for new cabinets</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>3. Choose Stock or Semi-Custom Cabinets</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Custom cabinets cost 2-3x more than semi-custom with minimal functional difference for most homeowners.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>4. Buy Appliances Yourself</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Contractors often mark up appliances 20-30%. Buy directly during holiday sales (Memorial Day, Black Friday, Labor Day) and save $1,000-$3,000.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>5. Do Your Own Demo</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">If you're handy, demolition is labor-intensive but not technically difficult. Doing it yourself saves $1,000-$2,500.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>What you'll need:</b> - Dumpster rental ($400-$800) - Basic tools (pry bars, hammer, utility knife) - Safety gear (gloves, goggles, dust mask) - 1-3 days of hard work</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>6. Choose Quartz Over Marble</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Quartz looks nearly identical to marble but costs 30-50% less and requires no maintenance.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>7. Limit Tile Patterns</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Simple tile layouts (subway, herringbone) cost less in labor than intricate mosaics or custom patterns.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>8. Paint Cabinets Instead of Replacing</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Professional cabinet painting costs $3,000-$8,000 vs. $10,000-$30,000 for new cabinets. If your cabinets are structurally sound, this is a huge savings.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>9. Use Open Shelving Strategically</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Open shelves cost significantly less than upper cabinets. Use them for 20-30% of upper storage to save $1,000-$3,000.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>10. Get Multiple Quotes</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">This is obvious but critical. Three quotes from licensed, insured contractors will show you the market range and highlight outliers.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline Expectations: How Long Should It Take?</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Understanding timeline helps you spot contractors who are padding hours or dragging out projects.</span></p>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Small Kitchen (70-100 sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline:</b> 3-5 weeks</span></p>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 1: Demo, rough plumbing/electrical</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 2: Drywall repair, cabinet installation</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 3: Countertops templated and installed</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 4: Flooring, backsplash, painting</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 5: Final trim, appliances, punch list</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Medium Kitchen (100-150 sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline:</b> 4-7 weeks</span></p>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 1: Demo and rough work</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 2-3: Plumbing/electrical, cabinets</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 4: Countertops</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 5: Flooring and backsplash</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 6: Painting and trim</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 7: Appliances, fixtures, final touches</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0d4e36; -webkit-text-stroke: #0d4e36"><span class="s1"><b>Large Kitchen (150-200+ sq ft)</b></span></h3>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Timeline:</b> 6-10 weeks</span></p>
<ul class="ul1">
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 1-2: Demo, structural work, rough plumbing/electrical</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 3-4: Cabinet installation</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 5: Countertop template and installation</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 6-7: Flooring, backsplash</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 8: Painting, trim work</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 9: Appliance installation, final electrical/plumbing</span></li>
  <li class="li6"><span class="s2"></span><span class="s1">Week 10: Punch list and final inspection</span></li>
</ul>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Red flag:</b> If a contractor says a small kitchen will take 12 weeks, they're either overbooked (working on multiple jobs simultaneously) or padding the timeline.</span></p>
<p class="p1"><span class="s1"></span><br></p>
<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Verify Your Kitchen Remodel Quote</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">You've got the numbers. You know what each component should cost. But analyzing a 15-page quote with dozens of line items is still overwhelming.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">That's exactly why we built <b>Ungouge.ai</b>.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>How it works:</b> 1. <b>Upload your kitchen remodel quote</b> - Any format: PDF, spreadsheet, photo, email 2. <b>Our AI analyzes every line item</b> - We compare materials, labor rates, and markups to real market data 3. <b>Get a detailed breakdown</b> - See exactly what's fair, what's high, and where you're potentially being overcharged 4. <b>No email required, no sales pitch</b> - We're not connecting you with contractors or generating leads. Just giving you the truth.</span></p>
